=== scripts/run_m4_live.py --help ===
usage: run_m4_live.py [-h] [--config CONFIG] --out OUT [--execute-live]
                      [--approval-id APPROVAL_ID]

Explicitly authorized local Qwen/llama.cpp executor for the frozen M4-v2
schedule.

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --config CONFIG
  --out OUT             new run directory beneath runs/m4; raw artifacts stay
                        local and ACL-restricted
  --execute-live        required explicit live-inference switch; omitted by
                        default
  --approval-id APPROVAL_ID
                        operator's separate approval reference; does not
                        itself authorize a future run
=== scripts/audit_m4_live.py --help ===
usage: audit_m4_live.py [-h] --run RUN [--config CONFIG]

Independently replay live M4 settlements and raw request/response links.

options:
  -h, --help       show this help message and exit
  --run RUN
  --config CONFIG  optional frozen live runtime config; defaults to checked-in
                   v3
=== scripts/run_sprint_monitor.py --help ===
usage: run_sprint_monitor.py [-h] [--config CONFIG] [--out OUT]
                             [--mode {mock,live}] [--approval-id APPROVAL_ID]

Bounded B2-B5 dispatcher; default and only current mode is offline mock.

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --config CONFIG
  --out OUT
  --mode {mock,live}
  --approval-id APPROVAL_ID
=== scripts/audit_sprint_monitor_live.py --help ===
usage: audit_sprint_monitor_live.py [-h] --run RUN [--config CONFIG]
                                    [--out OUT]

Offline replay of a saved Sprint Monitor live run; never performs inference.

options:
  -h, --help       show this help message and exit
  --run RUN
  --config CONFIG
  --out OUT
